model {
  extend basalt.modelGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "The disabled runtime-slot controller owns active selection in runtime-slots-v1 storage beside existing ownership and membership records. The live stack evaluates no extra resource, exports no runtime class, and adds no binding, migration or release declaration. Promotion also binds the current controller release and source input independently of stable controller and runtime identity. Exact execution identity scopes stream accounting and health watchers across repeated use of the same logical slot. A future private slot driver must bind provider application, version, logical instance, immutable image and process boot separately from the stable controller identity. Candidate startup never calls the active runtime lifecycle. Promotion collects fresh health and every current native-policy acknowledgement, dirty or clean, outside storage transactions, then compares complete membership and selection in one transaction and commits selection with its receipt. Expired candidate acknowledgements cannot borrow a renewed desired deadline. Retired membership denials stay in the policy digest and promotion revision receipt, and every candidate must acknowledge their fresh dirty empty projections. Clean live policies must be unexpired. A dirty live policy, such as a pool that is not ready, vetoes only that pool in the runtime scheduler and slot router; runtime-wide proofs and recovery install it with a fresh lease, and its revision stays in the digest compared at commit. An uncertain started promotion permits inspection only. Admission leases register before authority or signing and identify their selected slot before dispatch. Each runtime's readiness may report its measured distance to the database, location and measurement state; the health read carries them as closed values and an image without them is unknown. Model routing prefers runtimes within twenty milliseconds of the database while they are under the growth target, then far and unknown runtimes under it, then the rest, keeping the root's tie preference within a tier; without distances the order is unchanged and no ready runtime becomes unroutable. Fleet rows record the reported distance for the fleet read, active-health carries the root's, and each cell admission logs one closed placement decision. Revocation persists dirty state and aborts pool streams before all active, candidate and draining slots acknowledge, or an explicit durable controller fence denies routing and closes that slot's streams. An unknown or unfenced non-acknowledging slot prevents writer acknowledgement. Private runtime request boundaries decode invalid input and identity into typed refusals with closed reasons. Unexpected defects return a sanitized correlated 500, retain the cause class only in logs, and cross the private binding without becoming refusals or repeating mutations. Signed admission does not require a forwarding identity header. Drivers have no public ingress. Per-slot health leases protect draining streams independently. Retirement waits for drain, targets the exact old boot and retains uncertainty without repeating destruction. Pre-adoption legacy request counts belong to the isolate that holds them, so a count left by a reset or redeployed isolate never holds a drain open; established legacy connections stay the drain proof. At most one inactive candidate or draining slot coexists with active serving. Switching back requires the same fresh policy and identity proof. Existing lifecycle code ignores the additive namespace. Provisioning, private runtime adapters, release admission and live reliance require their separate approved phase."
    }
  }
}
